# Backend

- All API routes under `app/(app)/api/`.
- Every route: `const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession()`; return `{ message: "..." }` on errors.
- Admin-only: also `isCurrentUserAdmin()` from `lib/roles.ts`. Moderators: use existing `isAdminOrModerator()` helpers where applicable.
- Domain logic in `lib/`; routes stay thin.
- `createClient()` for user scope; `createAdminClient()` for service role — never expose service role to the client.
- Single Sanity client: `@/sanity/lib/client` — no duplicate clients. Schemas in `sanity.config.ts`.
- Drive: `lib/google-drive.ts`; validate downloads against `drive_sources`; default mimeType to `application/octet-stream` when missing.
- Blob: `/api/blobs`, `/api/blobs/list` — session-gated; prefer server-side filtering when touching list routes.
- Migrations: `supabase/migrations/` — small, clear intent per PR.
- Rate limiting / monitoring: reuse `lib/rate-limit.ts`, `lib/monitoring.ts` where endpoints need protection.
- No `console.log`; `console.error` only in catch blocks for real errors. No `any`.
